==============================================================================
       G A M E   P A C K   2   ::   more classics, legal and free
==============================================================================
 Every one of these was made free by the people who own it: released as
 freeware, put in the public domain, or given away by the author. All the
 files come straight from the official homes listed below, untouched.
 All downloads are FREE (no ratio hit).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SCUMMVM ADVENTURES          SCUMMVM-WIN.ZIP / SCUMMVM-MAC.DMG + the games
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ScummVM (GNU GPL) runs the old point-and-click adventures on modern Macs
 and PCs. Get ScummVM for your machine, unzip a game into its own folder,
 then in ScummVM click Add Game... and pick that folder. These are the
 freeware games ScummVM itself hands out, by permission of their owners:

   BASS-CD.ZIP ......... Beneath a Steel Sky (1994), the full CD talkie
   LURE.ZIP ............ Lure of the Temptress (1992)
   FOTAQ.ZIP ........... Flight of the Amazon Queen (1995), talkie
   DRASCULA.ZIP ........ Drascula: The Vampire Strikes Back (1996)
   DRASCULA-AUDIO.ZIP .. Drascula's CD music, unzip it into the same folder
   DREAMWEB.ZIP ........ DreamWeb (1994), cyberpunk noir. Grown-up themes.
   NIPPON.ZIP .......... Nippon Safes, Inc. (1992)
   SOLTYS.ZIP .......... Soltys (1995)
   SFINX.ZIP ........... Sfinx (1997)
   GODTHUND.ZIP ........ God of Thunder (1993), Norse action-adventure
   MYSTHOUS.ZIP ........ Mystery House (1980), Sierra's very first game

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ZZT                          ZZT32.ZIP + ZETA-WIN.ZIP / ZETA-MAC.ZIP
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Tim Sweeney's ZZT (1991), the game that started Epic MegaGames, with all
 four original worlds. Epic re-licensed it in 1997 so it can be passed
 around free. Zeta (MIT license) runs it on modern machines: unzip both,
 then open ZZT.EXE with Zeta (or drop the ZZT folder on it).
 From the Museum of ZZT (museumofzzt.com) and zeta.asie.pl.

